WEBVTT

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:04.870
Infinite Ryvius

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.670
Hey, is it true that he
was admitted to the hospital?

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.880
I heard that he had a fight
with his brother, or something.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.310
And his brother beat him up? Really?

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:18.280
I thought he'd be a little stronger than that.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.680
He's weaker than he looks.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.550
Kouji's not much of a guy.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.260
U-Um, Kouji.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.760
It's almost time for your duty, but
it's okay, I'll take care of it for you.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.730
There's no need to go outta your
way for me. It's my responsibility.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:42.140
B-But...

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:49.340
Rescue should be arriving soon
as well, so it's only until then.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:53.340
In a few days, we'll be outta here.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.850
Then, I won't have to see his face...

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:57.810
Any longer.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.190
Infinite Ryvius

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:17.810
If you're going to walk, right here will be fine

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.810
Although loneliness...

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:26.150
...can sometimes be unbearable

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:33.380
There's the benefit of not hurting anyone...

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:38.460
...and the benefit of not being exposed...

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.430
...and hurt by others as well

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:48.960
At the opposite side of the frozen sea...

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.740
...the dream and the reality...

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:56.370
...that you saw cross paths

00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:00.070
Some light is shed...

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:04.650
...but how it is done is unknown...

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:11.890
...so that we can go to a different place

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:19.890
The things I want have no shape

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:28.300
Tear the final universe, today until tomorrow

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:42.460
My Moment

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:53.940
Gravity control?

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:58.570
Yes. The main functions of Ryvius
seem to be run by gravity control.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.210
That's impossible!

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.310
It's a fact.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:06.010
I had always thought of the Arcs Theory
to be an untested, impracticable theory.

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:08.920
So the Orbital Security
Bureau <i>is</i> after this ship.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.120
Then this is...!

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.090
Top secret.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:14.620
There's no way they'd hide such
a thing inside a Training Center.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:18.190
But if it were true, it would
explain their quick response.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:20.500
So you're saying that they
didn't come to rescue us?

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.000
Probably not.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.270
What puzzles me even further is,
why did Ryvius suddenly move?

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:27.070
Perhaps the system is unstable.

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:29.940
What's gonna happen to us?

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:34.510
Present depth, Sere 2, 790. Estimated
depth for control to kick in, 890.

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:39.050
Temperature of outer wall, 160 anvils.
Gravitational waves around Ryvius stable.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.150
Brian, what about the Solid?

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:41.980
I just loaded it.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:43.750
Charlie! Where were you?

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.050
You're so useless.

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:47.110
C-Come on.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.790
Okay, this should do.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.560
This is the first time I've put
together a Gravity Control Solid.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:56.100
If it wasn't for Kreis, it would've
taken us at least three days.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.930
Hey, what are you doing? We're done.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:01.640
Th-This is unbelievable. I
found it! I finally found it!

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:02.840
What is it?

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:06.640
Look. I found the instructions
for the system found in W86.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.980
What was all that shaking?

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:10.770
The ship probably bumped into
some debris or something.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:13.610
My neck.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:18.490
My cake...!

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:20.720
Why not just have her make another one?

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:23.120
Sure. Anything you'd like, let me know.

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:25.890
I continue to clean, but it's endless.

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:28.200
Can't those Zwei guys control
this ship a little better?

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.770
Why should we have to do this?

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.800
Tell me. What happened?

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:32.900
What do you mean?

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:34.000
What happened to Kouji?

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.540
Why not ask him directly?

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:37.610
He wouldn't tell me!

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:38.770
Yeah, you have a point.

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:40.410
It was Yuki, wasn't it?

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:42.480
He keeps things to himself too much.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:45.780
You've known Kouji since he
was little, haven't you, Aoi?

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:47.650
Are those brothers always like that?

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:49.250
I don't really know.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.920
We were in different classes
during Middle School.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:54.590
I remember though, after returning
from home stay, for whatever reason...

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:57.020
...the two were in a furious fight.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:00.050
Ever since then, they haven't gotten along.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.050
I'm beginning to find this interesting.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:02.930
What?

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:04.520
The story on Kouji Aiba.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:07.990
Find something?

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:09.200
Nothing.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.710
There's nothing wrong with
the respective cables.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.610
Air adjustments are
functioning as programmed.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:16.180
Then we're done here.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.110
Mind if I ask you something?

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.280
Go ahead.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:21.880
Why are you together with Nicks?

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.880
Because he pulls me along, I guess.

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:31.060
For instance, I owe it to him
that I'm talking to you like this.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.230
It's less effort on my part.

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.700
Less effort?

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:37.470
You don't know what <i>you</i> want to do?

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.570
Are you all right with that?

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:42.800
Well, isn't there anything you
want to do? Plans for yourself?

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:45.040
I think that's a different subject.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:45.840
It's not at all different.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:49.840
But Kouji, you're pulled along by Ikumi.

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:53.850
Sorry. Am I wrong?

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.040
I wonder. I never thought about it.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.380
Kouji.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:03.620
When Kouji was little,
his parents were divorced...

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.050
...so Kouji sort of took on the
role of being Yuki's father.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:09.690
The two were always together.

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:13.000
They're fortunate to even have parents.

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:18.230
It's good that the ship has
stabilized, but what do we do now?

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:22.370
If people found out we sunk into the
Geduld again, it would sure cause panic.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:25.280
We should refrain from making an
announcement for the time being.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:27.480
We don't want any panic.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:29.780
Okay! Re-ascend Ryvius!

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:31.980
We'll send out rescue signals again!

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:35.180
You've gotta be kidding! It was
tough enough just stopping this!

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:37.290
Loading the ascending program right now.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:39.220
S-Sure.

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:40.600
How long do you think it'll take?

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:44.460
We're basing it on the sub-surface
program, so... 8 hours should do it.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:45.560
Okay.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:53.930
Matching aim with estimated filter.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:59.040
Don't let the target expose itself to
ordinary space. Keep it in the Geduld.

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:00.950
Prepare to release depth charges.

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:03.250
Roger. Will prepare to
release depth charges.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.690
Will Conrad be coming?

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:08.380
I know better than anyone
how persistent that man is.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:11.750
If we provide him with the
stage, he'll be sure to respond.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:15.020
We'll be using DUs for our depth
charges. Shell coating, level 7.

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:17.460
Activating acceleration container.

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:19.690
Output increased to 80 giga joules.

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:21.270
Charge!

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:22.440
Damn! Get him!

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:24.030
You can't do it!

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:34.780
Hurray! Congratulations!

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:37.010
Darn it! I tuned it wrong.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:39.720
Number 4 gets curry again today.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.350
What? They're really slacking off.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.190
Sorry. Did you wait long?

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:43.890
Forever!

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:49.900
You'd be better off forgetting about her.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:52.030
Huh? But... but...

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:57.030
<i>Because he pulls me along, I guess.</i>

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:02.570
<i>But Kouji, you're pulled along by Ikumi.</i>

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:07.510
<i>It's not like I'm being guided by</i>
<i>lkumi. I'm thinking for myself.</i>

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:11.620
<i>Just, every time, something happens.</i>

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:15.890
What did you do that for?

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:16.620
Here you go.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:21.900
Did something happen again?

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:24.300
Nothing happened. So don't stick around me.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:25.970
What kinda attitude is that?

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:26.700
What?

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:30.930
You're not hurt too badly.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.210
Ow.

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:34.610
Really? Then I'll bring
some medicine to treat it.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:36.240
Don't bother!

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:37.680
<i>This is what I mean.</i>

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:42.750
<i>Areas 1 through 26 will enter shift B.</i>

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:46.150
<i>All those in transit are advised</i>
<i>to practice extra caution.</i>

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:50.590
We're in Sere 2?

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.760
We've gone back into the Geduld?

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:54.700
That's not even funny for a joke.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:57.300
Charlie! What are you guys thinking?

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.700
R-Ryvius suddenly moved on its own.

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:05.260
But there's no reason to worry.
We've stabilized the ship.

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:07.200
Who the hell do you think you guys are?

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:10.210
Why aren't you telling everyone?
What's the big idea?

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:12.040
W-Well...!

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:14.850
Hey, Charlie.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:20.020
There are no secrets between us, right?

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:23.610
The fact is... the Zwei members...!

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:26.630
See? Super, don't you think?

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:30.260
A developed version of a
high-speed spaceship. Interesting.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.160
If I can work at the core of this, I'm
confident that I can take it into flight.

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:36.430
I'm okay with that, but what
will we do about the crew?

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.700
Give me the top four Level Two guys.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:44.170
All right. I'll put you in charge
of that. I'm counting on you.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:47.980
Hey!

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:54.690
It's so we can escape in a
worst-case scenario, fool.

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:02.500
Ow.

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:04.000
Does it hurt?

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:05.230
Just a bit.

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:06.960
Aoi was quite worried about you.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:09.200
Oh.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:11.110
You're pretty clumsy at
handling these things.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:13.810
It would probably be so much easier
if I were as lighthearted as you are.

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:15.710
Then why not be so yourself?

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:19.280
Ikumi! Your ID card received a page!

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:19.880
From who?

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:20.780
The Zwei guys.

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:21.680
I wonder what it is.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:24.090
Thanks for the shampoo.

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.210
Not a problem.

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:30.320
Come to think of it, Faina's
never joined us in the shower.

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:34.360
I understand that she's received permission
from Zwei for a private bathroom.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.960
Why?

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:39.130
Maybe because she's embarrassed
to expose her small breasts.

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:42.600
Oh! Or maybe she's got
birthmarks on her butt.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:44.510
Don't be silly!

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:46.140
In her case she has her reasons.

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:47.180
Reasons?

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:51.580
Yes. Did you know? She's
from Titania, Uranus.

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:53.050
- What?
- You're kidding!

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:54.720
Your time's up, you know.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:56.080
Right away!

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:30.180
Bye.

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:31.450
Please take over for us.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:32.280
Sure. Bye.

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:35.920
The gravitational field has been
reduced due to decreasing the output.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:38.590
The center pillar clinging to
the ship is starting to melt.

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:39.960
What?

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:43.230
In approximately 6 hours, the radiation
within Liebel will reach a level of D-4.

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:45.500
The killers we captured are still on Liebel.

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:47.500
Shall we call back Juli and the others?

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:48.900
There should be no need for that.

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:51.710
Just think of how many lives were
lost because of those criminals.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:53.140
We'll be ascending in a moment.

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:55.130
We have no obligation to risk
our lives in order to save them.

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:04.880
Infinite Ryvius

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:09.990
Infinite Ryvius

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:13.390
Welcome, everyone.

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:15.560
I'm Gran McDaniel of Zwei.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:21.140
I have gathered you in hopes that you
will work with us to learn to operate...

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:22.270
<i>...this</i> system!

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:23.610
What's this?

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:25.370
You want us to move this robot?

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:28.210
That's right. This Vital Guarder.

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:31.050
It looks like fun, but
rescue's arriving soon, right?

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:32.010
There's no reason for this.

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:33.850
I told you to help! You're gonna help!

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:36.150
What gives you the right
to order us around?

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.080
Stop it.

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:39.890
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:41.950
N-No, <i>I'm</i> sorry. I
wasn't paying attention.

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.290
It's okay. I'll do it.

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:46.690
No, let me. It was my fault.

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:49.330
Um... that...!

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:53.230
Why, you're... Faina.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:57.630
Kouji? What happened to you?

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:01.170
A little something.

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:20.690
Why should we have to do this?

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:23.060
Really. This is dumb.

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:26.430
Stop complaining. It's not every day you
can get your hands on something like this.

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:34.800
Yuki Aiba.

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:38.040
I believe we now meet for the
fourth time. I'm Ikumi Oze, 16.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.680
No one asked you.

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:42.120
How heartless. We're on the same team.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:43.850
You guys put me there
without my knowledge.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:45.950
Stop hating your brother so much.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:48.660
You give the impression of
suffering from "brother complex."

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:51.320
I can see right through you. From
your attitude, and your words.

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:54.830
You try to look like a rebel, but all
you're doing is frustrating yourself...

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:57.570
...doing as you wish, and
causing trouble for others.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:59.330
And in the end, you regret your actions.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:00.540
Am I wrong?

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:04.370
Why are you jumping to conclusions?
Do you read people's minds or something?

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:06.440
When it comes to your mind, I believe so.

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:07.410
What a joker!

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:10.710
In a fight with your brother?

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:13.880
Actually, you can hardly call it a
fight. It was completely one-sided.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:21.390
My parents divorced when we were little...

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:25.050
...I've been looking out for him since,
but now, well, he's like this.

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:28.200
It doesn't matter what I say, he always
finds a reason to snap back at me.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:30.160
He's gotta realize, he's
no longer a little kid.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:34.300
I just can't figure out why he does it.

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:35.600
Do you hate your brother?

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:37.570
So much that I'd wish he'd disappear.

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:39.730
Are you saying that from your heart?

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:45.710
I suggest you find the chance
to have a good talk with him.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:51.510
<i>But his fist talks quicker than his mouth.</i>

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:56.860
Hey! What's going on there? Stop it!

00:14:56.860 --> 00:14:57.760
Which do you bet on?

00:14:57.760 --> 00:14:59.590
Not interested.

00:14:59.590 --> 00:15:03.550
He walks off with everything! With
his carefree grin, every single thing!

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:05.230
So you take things out on him?

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:06.930
It has nothing to do with you!

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:10.240
We're on the same team, so
it has a lot to do with me!

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:11.510
Get serious!

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:13.530
You're the one that needs to get serious!

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:16.710
Don't think I've forgotten
about what happened back then!

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:22.110
You're being a pest! Are you
no different from my brother?

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:29.250
Is that the only way you see things?
You're warped. You damn baby!

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:06.730
No!

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:17.540
My costume!

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:21.240
I'm scared!

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:22.140
Juli!

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:23.680
They're depth charges
coming from ordinary space!

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:26.010
What? Stay here!

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:27.420
- No!
- Pat!

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:28.470
No way!

00:16:28.850 --> 00:16:32.790
This is section W86! Bridge,
answer me! What just happened?

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:37.080
An incredible number of shadows appeared
on the radar. They came from above us.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:38.280
Enemy attack?

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:46.330
Again. Why is it moving on its own?

00:16:48.800 --> 00:16:49.570
I'm scared.

00:16:53.980 --> 00:16:54.840
I'm scared.

00:16:56.980 --> 00:16:57.570
I'm scared!

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:03.820
Are we being attacked from outside?

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:06.420
Allies of the men who attacked the bridge?

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:08.860
I can't be sure, but probably.

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:09.690
Hurry!

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:10.820
Ikumi!

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:12.820
What do you mean, "enemy attack"?

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:17.030
The output won't increase?

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:18.900
What are the maintenance guys doing?

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:23.940
W-We've gotta escape. Hurry!

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:27.640
We can't. There are charges in
every direction Ryvius could go.

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:29.870
Cancel the Solid and prepare to submerge!

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:32.150
Juli! You mustn't bring kids to the...!

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:35.010
Are you suggesting we submerge from
our present depth of Sere 2, 800?

00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:39.320
If we increase our gravitational field,
we might reduce the effect of Geduld.

00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:42.160
But Chic and the others have
gone to the engine room.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:45.320
We'd be wiped out by the charges before
we could rewrite the Solid without them.

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:48.460
What's the situation?

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:50.630
What a relief. We need your help.

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:51.670
They want our help.

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.730
What do they have in mind?

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:55.800
We're gonna cancel the
Solid, and submerge!

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:58.240
We're sinking into Geduld again? Why?

00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:00.630
- You must explain to us...!
- Understand the situation.

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:06.780
A coded message received
from communication V...

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:08.380
...by way of Iridium U 6549.

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:09.480
It's from Captain Conrad.

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:11.210
He's responded.

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:17.720
We must stop Bratica,
no matter what it takes.

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:19.490
Prepare to fire torpedoes.

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:26.030
This is too complicated.

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:27.930
Is this what Zwei can do?

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:30.800
Cancelled!

00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:35.230
This one too. This Solid...
...is it Gravity Control?

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:37.040
Let's see...

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:37.810
Here.

00:18:37.810 --> 00:18:38.940
Ah, sorry.

00:18:44.050 --> 00:18:45.020
It stopped.

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:46.050
Did we get through?

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:48.960
No, we're momentarily in an open area.
Attacks will start again in seven minutes!

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.660
Eins. What about the people in Liebel?

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:53.990
Th-They should be under Charlie's care.

00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:55.950
Then they should be fine.

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:04.270
Are you going out with him?

00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:06.430
I'm asking you if you're
going out with my brother.

00:19:06.970 --> 00:19:08.700
Are you Kouji's...?

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:10.850
I'm the one asking a question!

00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:12.950
They only met a short while ago!

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:14.780
You shut up!
Well, answer me.

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:17.210
<i>Bastard.</i>

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:21.120
Solid cancellation complete.

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:22.090
Good!

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:24.290
Commence Ryvius submersion!

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:25.830
Something's coming from below!

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:26.790
Check it out at once!

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:28.060
You're a Zwei member, right?

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:29.120
Check it yourself!

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:33.570
Bosscon class?

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:34.300
Torpedoes?

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:35.300
Is it programmed for a specific depth?

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:37.470
No, likely set to go off close to the ship.

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:39.410
Can't we descend any quicker?

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:40.740
We have no time.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:42.210
Torpedoes...

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:44.910
Stop it! What did we do to you
people to deserve this, anyway?

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:48.820
Why should we have to suffer this way?

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:50.880
What is this? What's going on?

00:19:53.220 --> 00:19:53.920
We're gonna die.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:55.010
Noooo!

00:19:57.160 --> 00:20:00.560
Wait! This ship has more
than 400 people on board.

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:03.830
If that Solid we saw is real,
there must be a way outta this!

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:05.600
There is!

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:06.860
There's a way?

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:22.510
Torpedoes will reach target in 7,
6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1. Reached target.

00:20:27.220 --> 00:20:29.020
Target has been hit.

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:31.720
- Fire neutrino pinger!
- Sir?

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:34.050
Functions have been affected
from the depth charge attack.

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:41.200
Functions recovered.

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:43.070
We have something on the
pinger. It's Bratica!

00:20:43.070 --> 00:20:43.970
Can't be!

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:46.410
We'll pursue it. Chase it into T32.

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:51.510
No damages. Ryvius descending.

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:54.050
As anticipated, we're not
affected at all by the Geduld.

00:20:54.050 --> 00:20:56.880
The gravitational field kicked
in, just in time, didn't it.

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:59.190
I wouldn't have imagined
it would go this well.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:01.150
We're saved.

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:27.380
There are no signs that anyone went
to rescue the people on Liebel.

00:21:27.380 --> 00:21:28.580
Really?

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:29.840
Damn Zwei.

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:37.690
Target has descended past Sere 3, 500.

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:39.530
Target's gone beyond our attack range.

00:21:39.530 --> 00:21:42.300
Continuing with this
pursuit will be dangerous.

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:45.200
There is less than two hours
until the Neutrino Burst arrives.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:47.170
Unless we move, we'll be swept away.

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:50.470
We'll retrieve the training ship that
separated from Bratica, and ascend.

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:51.500
Roger.

00:22:07.140 --> 00:22:11.410
In your dry eyes...

00:22:11.410 --> 00:22:16.480
...a silhouette appears

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:21.190
The blue colored future...

00:22:21.190 --> 00:22:27.290
...swayed and glittered

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.340
Ah... No one wants...

00:22:37.340 --> 00:22:45.950
...freedom out of pity

00:22:45.950 --> 00:22:54.390
Ah... To the days I feared...

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:58.290
...that I'd end up hurting someone,

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:04.660
goodbye

00:23:08.690 --> 00:23:10.860
Infinite Ryvius

00:23:10.860 --> 00:23:12.120
Next episode: The Changing Times
Airs Blue.

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:15.060
Next episode: The Changing Times
With the appearance of this man,
Ryvius encounters a violent shock.

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:15.690
Next episode: The Changing Times

00:23:15.690 --> 00:23:18.760
Next episode: The Changing Times
The new order increases
the distance between Yuki and I...

00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:19.030
Next episode: The Changing Times

00:23:19.030 --> 00:23:21.470
Next episode: The Changing Times
...and decreases the
distance between Faina and I.

00:23:21.470 --> 00:23:23.600
Next episode: The Changing Times
The changing times trifle with me.

00:23:23.600 --> 00:23:24.470
Next episode: The Changing Times

00:23:24.470 --> 00:23:25.040
Next episode: The Changing Times
This cannot...!

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:25.910
Next episode: The Changing Times

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:28.140
Next episode: The Changing Times
This cannot be my fate.

00:23:28.140 --> 00:23:28.830
Next episode: The Changing Times
